A. The 2-Month Summer Internship (The Premier Route)
Arcesium relies heavily on its summer internship pipeline to lock in full-time talent before the final year of college begins. They recruit interns to work across their major Indian engineering centers in Hyderabad, Bengaluru, and Gurugram.

The Conversion Engine: If you clear the summer internship interviews and build optimized, production-ready backend tools or data systems for your team, you stand a massive chance of getting a Pre-Placement Offer (PPO).

The Advantage: Getting a PPO ensures you start your final year with a premium product-company offer already in hand, saving you from the pressure of final-year mass placement drives.

B. The 6-Month Winter Internship Pipeline
For campuses or students whose academic rules support extended final-semester training, Arcesium rolls out 6-month technical internship drives. These roles place interns straight into intense infrastructure development, data architecture, or UI/UX engineering tracks, providing a direct evaluation corridor to transition seamlessly into a full-time SDE-I role upon graduation.
